## Program Constraints

- Hybrid SQLite remains canonical; the hosted service stays a read-only projection.
- Document lifecycle, outcome disposition, reconciliation, and recursive closure remain explicit
  independent dimensions. Labels and gates must not imply equivalence.
- Historical repair is manifest-driven and supervised when residual work, descendants, or intent
  are ambiguous.
- Closure records and rollups are derived; repair acts through their governing document, outcome,
  relationship, evidence, and reconciliation authorities.
- Completed PRM-0039 and MAP-0028 remain immutable historical evidence of the escaped gate.
- IDEA-0021 remains active and unrelated unless separate evidence changes its state.

## Verification Strategy

- Exercise fresh and upgraded fixtures that reproduce safe drift, open descendants, residual work,
  body/database disagreement, queued campaigns, and multi-role closure lookup.
- Assert plan/apply idempotence, stale-token refusal, rollback/retry safety, and checkpoint/rebuild
  parity.
- Compare canonical local state, loop findings, closure projections, reporter payloads, hosted view
  models, and browser-visible summaries exactly.
- Separate Work3 candidate qualification from Work5 publication and production reconciliation.

## Next Route

Execute CAMP-0159 as the bounded M1 Work2 campaign. Do not run historical repair or production
delivery inside M1.
